{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"THIRD independent observation, 2026-08-07 — with a sharper signature than the first two.\n\nChanges 1493 (ticket 13b4) and 1496 (ticket ccf6): the bot skipped BOTH uploads. 1493 sat **70 minutes** at LLM-Review=0 while the bot **voted on NEWER changes in the same window** (1497). So this is not the bot being down, saturated, or strictly FIFO-backlogged — it processes later arrivals while an earlier change waits indefinitely. That rules out 'slow queue' as the explanation.\n\nRemedy that worked: a NO-OP REBASE + re-push produced a vote within 5 minutes on both changes. Note this is a different trigger from the `recheck-review` comment that unstuck 1486 and 1490 — so at least two distinct nudges revive a stalled change, which suggests the review is queued on an EVENT the original upload failed to emit (or that was dropped), rather than on the change's state.\n\nRunning tally of the same defect this session:\n* 1486 (599e) — both uploads skipped; needed `recheck-review`\n* 1490 (e7a9) — no vote on upload; `recheck-review` at 11:41 produced a vote at 11:44\n* 1493, 1496 (13b4, ccf6) — both skipped; 70-minute stall with newer changes overtaking; fixed by no-op rebase\n\nFour changes, three agents, two different manual nudges. This is reproducible, not incidental.\n\nAdditional diagnostic value in the overtaking behaviour: whatever queues the review clearly still works for SOME uploads in the same period, so the fault is in the per-upload trigger path, not in the reviewer or its worker pool. That should substantially narrow the root-cause search called for in AC1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786108129339771001,"uuid":"21365716-c8d0-4f1b-8dc0-621c18da3a6c"}